Sat Oct 24 04:45:34 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 1.15.1:
  * New RaBitQ quantization with FastScan and multi-bit support
  * New EDEN and TurboQuant quantizers, SuperKMeans clustering
  * New Metal GPU backend, RISC-V RVV and Arm SVE SIMD backends
  * New IndexIVFFlatPanorama family and cuVS IVF-SQ backend
  * Python type stubs, pip install support, wider C API coverage
  * HNSW speedups, similarity mode and persistent locks
  * Hardened index deserialization and many crash fixes
  * Support Python 3.13 and 3.14, build against numpy 2
  * Many more fixes and improvements; see upstream's release notes
    for the full list
- Spec file cleanup (spec-cleaner); drop the redundant /usr/faiss
  staging install, package the new per-level C API libraries
- Drop the obsolete libfaiss_python_callbacks.so symlink: the callbacks
  library is static in 1.15.x, nothing ships the shared object, and the
  non-idempotent %post broke installing both Python flavors together

